# Casualty_Age_Ratio
# Feature description: Calculates the ratio of Age_of_Driver to Age_of_Casualty, representing relative age dynamics in accidents.
# Usefulness: Highlights intergenerational dynamics in accidents and could provide insights into driver and casualty sex correlation during incidents.
df['Casualty_Age_Ratio'] = df['Age_of_Driver'] / (df['Age_of_Casualty'] + 1e-5)  # Add small epsilon to avoid division by zero
end

python
# High_Risk_Age_Flag
# Feature description: Binary flag indicating whether the driver’s age is below 25 or above 65, considering these age groups are typically associated with higher accident risks.
# Usefulness: These groups are known for higher accident probabilities given their typically lower experience (younger drivers) or delayed reaction times (older drivers), potentially correlating with driver sex.
df['High_Risk_Age_Flag'] = ((df['Age_of_Driver'] < 25) | (df['Age_of_Driver'] > 65)).astype(int)
end

