Impact\n# Feature description: Combines Number_of_Casualties with Vehicle_Type to encode potential differences in accident severity associated with different vehicle types.\n# Usefulness: Reveals how vehicle type affects casualty count, which could vary by the driver’s sex due to vehicle preference or behavioral factors.\ndf['Vehicle_Casualty_Impact'] = df['Number_of_Casualties'] * df['Vehicle_Type']", "# Casualty_Severity_Normalized\n# Feature description: Scales Casualty_IMD_Decile using min-max normalization for consistent representation.\n# Usefulness: Enables easier comparisons of socioeconomic impacts, capturing differences in driver demographics across regions.\ndf['Casualty_Severity_Normalized'] = (df['Casualty_IMD_Decile'] - df['Casualty_IMD_Decile'].min()) / (df['Casualty_IMD_Decile'].max() - df['Casualty_IMD_Decile'].min())", "# Driver_Casualty_Age_Band_Difference\n# Feature description: Calculates the difference between Age_Band_of_Driver and Age_Band_of_Casualty.\n# Usefulness: Simplifies age relationships into broad bands, highlighting generational dynamics that may correlate with driver sex.\ndf['Driver_Casualty_Age_Band_Difference'] = df['Age_Band_of_Driver'] - df['Age_Band_of_Casualty']", "# Number_of_Vehicles_Normalized\n# Feature description: Normalizes the Number_of_Vehicles in the accident using min-max scaling.\n# Usefulness: Ensures fair contribution in modeling by normalizing the accident size, enabling better representation of correlation to driver demographics.\ndf['Number_of_Vehicles_Normalized'] = (df['Number_of_Vehicles'] - df['Number_of_Vehicles'].min()) / (df['Number_of_Vehicles'].max() - df['Number_of_Vehicles'].min())", "# Drop Less Relevant Columns\n# Remove columns that are less likely to contribute significantly to driver sex prediction based on attributes and prior inspection.\ndf.drop(columns=['Pedestrian_Location', 'Pedestrian_Movement', 'Casualty_Type', \n                 'Vehicle_Location-Restricted_Lane', 'Casualty_Reference'], inplace=True)"]
